Option 1: Application Server (EC2/VM)

Example:

Java Spring Boot App
Tomcat/JBoss
Docker Compose or standalone Docker

Pros:
Easier to understand each component.
Less Kubernetes complexity.
Good for learning Prometheus scraping, Grafana dashboards, ELK, and Jaeger basics.

Cons:
Not how most production cloud-native applications are monitored.
Manual configuration.
Doesn't teach Kubernetes monitoring.



Option 2: Kubernetes (Helm)

Example:

Application
      │
      ▼
 Kubernetes
      │
 ├── Prometheus
 ├── Grafana
 ├── Alertmanager
 ├── Headlamp
 ├── EFK
 ├── Jaeger
 └── Node Exporter

Everything is installed using Helm.

Pros:
✔ Production standard
✔ Easier upgrades

helm upgrade
helm rollback
helm uninstall

✔ Industry practice
EKS
AKS
GKE
OpenShift

almost every Kubernetes platform uses Helm.



Metrics:        Prometheus + Grafana + Alertmanager 
Dashboard:      Headlamp
Logs:           EFK, ELK
Traces:         Jaeger
